-day orbit. Because of the motion of the Sun in relation to the barycentre of the Solar System, on 11 July Neptune was also not at its exact discovery position in relation to the Sun; if the more common heliocentric coordinate system is used, the discovery longitude was reached on 12 July 2011.\n\n[Question]\nUsing the heliocentric coordinate system, when did Neptune reach the discovery longitude? ","hint":"Find the sentence in the passage that uses the same key idea as the question.","answer":"12 July 2011","explanation":"Because of the motion of the Sun in relation to the barycentre of the Solar System, on 11 July Neptune was also not at its exact discovery position in relation to the Sun; if the more common heliocentric coordinate system is used, the discovery longitude was reached on 12 July 2011.","tags":["영어 독해","reading comprehension","Neptune","SQuAD","CC BY-SA 4.0"],"source_name":"Stanford Question Answering Dataset (SQuAD)","source_author":"Pranav Rajpurkar, Jian Zhang, Konstantin Lopyrev, and Percy Liang","source_url":"https://rajpurkar.github.io/SQuAD-explorer/","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Adapted from the Stanford Question Answering Dataset (SQuAD), licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0. Passage sources originate from Wikipedia; original English text retained."}]$problem_data$::jsonb) as item(
